 of the replies to this clip says, does this mean the Cleveland Cavaliers were also genuinely ","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:30:14+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:30:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/michael-bailey/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/mDxKZwasKLwo/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/mDxKZwasKLwo/","articleBody":"I’m not running a caption competition tonight but if I was … this would be the image.Ad if you did fancy submitting a caption, the inbox is always open: live@theathletic.com","headline":"Add your captions!","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:25:13+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:25:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/michael-bailey/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/mDxKZwasKLwo_7jb0RFpDc5nS_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/VXU6fNseAjul/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/VXU6fNseAjul/","articleBody":"Here’s some of the immediate reaction from those Eastern Conference champion Knicks.","headline":"Here’s some of the immediate reaction from those Eastern Conference champion Knicks.","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:20:13+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:20:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/michael-bailey/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/A2kYctnHhgmP/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/A2kYctnHhgmP/","articleBody":"The Knicks have reached the NBA Finals for the first time since 1999, as they demolished the Cavaliers with a Game 4 rout in Cleveland.New York’s 130-93 win completed a historic sweep, with all four games won by double digits and Jalen Brunson awarded the series MVP.But Game 4 was particularly painful for Cleveland, who looked forlorn and defensively accommodating throughout. The Knicks now wait to see whether the Oklahoma City Thunder or San Antonio Spurs come out on top in a Western Conference finals series tied up 2-2.Share your thoughts: live@theathletic.com","headline":"Knicks sweep Cavs with Game 4 dominance  ","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:16:26+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-25T18:08:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/michael-bailey/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/6dSEx7bO7H4Z/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/6dSEx7bO7H4Z/","articleBody":"New York’s dominant run has made the franchise feel invincible. The Knicks dropped the first two of three games to the Hawks in the first round and have been on as dominant a postseason run as there has been in NBA history. They go into the NBA Finals having won 11 straight playoff games.As far as confidence goes, New York has plenty of it going into the sport’s most prestigious stage. They’ll need all the confidence they can get. The Knicks can beat either Oklahoma City or San Antonio, but it won’t be as easy as their path in the Eastern Conference has made it seem.Neither the Thunder nor the Spurs has anyone in their starting lineup that the Knicks can hunt defensively. The Hawks had CJ McCollum and Jalen Johnson. The 76ers had Joel Embiid and Tyrese Maxey. The Cleveland Cavaliers had James Harden and Donovan Mitchell.New York’s potent offense is going to come back to a more realistic ground in the NBA Finals but it has the defense, just like whichever team it will face next, to make up for the inevitable drop off.","headline":"Takeaways: Can Knicks do this vs. Thunder or Spurs?","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:15:42+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:15:30+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/james-l-edwards-iii/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/Ij9PtNPHsu9v/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/Ij9PtNPHsu9v/","articleBody":"The final image of the 2025-26 Cleveland Cavaliers will be the team giving up at the end of Game 3 and fans of the New York Knicks storming their arena for an embarrassing Game 4.Making the conference finals is a noteworthy accomplishment for a franchise that for years couldn’t make it out of the second round, but the Cavs’ performance in this series was disastrous. Cleveland ended its season by playing 14 games in 27 days and coach Kenny Atkinson spent most of this series talking about fatigue and how tired his players were. Certainly, it played a role in how lopsided this series was — but that can’t be the excuse.Something has to change. But what? The Cavs are boxed in by their payroll and previous roster decisions. Nevertheless, the unvarnished truth is the team with the league’s highest payroll quit on their own floor to end their season. ","headline":"Takeaways: The Cavs quit","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:10:27+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:10:18+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/jason-lloyd/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Imagn Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Imagn Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/Ij9PtNPHsu9v_WE8O6UlUgW9w_1440x959.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Imagn Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/xknIbjR5hz5U/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/xknIbjR5hz5U/","articleBody":"Karl-Anthony Towns took 11 shots and yet, no one will sit here to complain about his lack of involvement. The Knicks wrecked the Cavaliers because of his — as he and Mike Brown have put it — “sacrifice.” Towns isn’t shooting as much. He continues to score efficiently. His passing is through the roof. And it’s transformed the Knicks offense in the process.For all the flak Towns gets about not being a malleable enough player, he continues to win. This is his third consecutive conference finals appearance, the first with the Minnesota Timberwolves and the last two with the Knicks. Now, he’s on the way to the NBA Finals for the first time.","headline":"Takeaways: Towns proves he’s a winner","dateModified":"2026-05-26T04:05:11+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T04:05:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/fred-katz/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Imagn Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Imagn Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/xknIbjR5hz5U_esX55nKjLqv0_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Imagn Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/gFP80iH9gDwh/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/gFP80iH9gDwh/","articleBody":"Small guards aren’t supposed to be able to win in the modern NBA.But Jalen Brunson keeps creating his own legacy. Watch my video on the Knicks’ star. ","headline":"Small guards aren’t supposed to be able to win in the modern NBA.But Jalen Brunson keeps creating hi","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:59:11+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:59:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/esfandiar-baraheni/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/vKigkqlVOVs9/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/vKigkqlVOVs9/","articleBody":"This Knicks regime’s first front-office hire was a little-known salary cap aficionado in Cleveland, Brock Aller.Leon Rose might be first in charge. William Wesley might be second. In 2020, Scott Perry was third; now, it’s Gersson Rosas. But Aller, an obsessor of the margins, someone who former Cavaliers lead executive David Griffin dubbed a “diabolical genius,” makes more trade calls than anyone else in the organization.And Aller adores his precious draft picks. One time, shortly after he joined the Knicks, Aller left an empty pizza box in his office for a curiously long time. A joke emerged in the building: That box must be where he stored the Knicks’ valuable first-rounders.The Mavericks, even with the Knicks all-in on Jalen Brunson, could not flip the lid of that pizza box.Four months later, after Brunson helped the Mavs to the conference finals, after Tom Thibodeau had hired Rick Brunson, they were rewarded.Aller swindled deal after deal on 2022 draft night, garnering future draft picks and getting off enough salary to sign Brunson and more.Four years later, Brunson is a three-time All-NBA member, the captain of a team that is just four victories short of inspiring New York City to combust.","headline":"Who is Brock Aller? The Brunson dealmaker","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:55:10+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:55:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/fred-katz/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/SLAIO8fs8Zu2/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/SLAIO8fs8Zu2/","articleBody":"For years, people claimed the Knicks could never win as long as owner James Dolan, who was more hands-on in his early stage of owning the franchise, was at the top. Those allegations can no longer exist, though the irony is that it took Dolan looking elsewhere for the front office to operate more autonomously.In 2018, Dolan’s passion project began in Las Vegas, the construction of a high-tech, globe-like venue on the Strip that would change entertainment forever. The process of building his Sphere was bumpy. The venture climbed over budget, ending up with a $2.3-billion price tag, which diverted much of Dolan’s time to Vegas. Basketball dropped down the list of priorities.Then the Sphere opened in 2023. He’s been around the team more since. Though his opinion was not the only factor in firing Tom Thibodeau just days after last year’s Eastern Conference finals, the deepest playoff run the Knicks had made in a quarter century, he spearheaded the coach’s ousting, as The Athletic’s Ian O’Connor detailed.Now, after three clinical series and a constant stream of innovative, strategic adjustments from the new head coach, Mike Brown, the Knicks will play deeper into the spring than they have since Dolan’s first year at the helm.The wager paid off.","headline":"Dolan’s role in recent Knicks run","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:52:50+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:52:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/fred-katz/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/vX3fXNwNI9UK/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/vX3fXNwNI9UK/","articleBody":"Our Knicks writer James L. Edwards III captured the scene inside Rocket Arena in Cleveland after the New York Knicks advance to the NBA Finals.","headline":"Scene inside Rocket Arena","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:49:10+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:49:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/lukas-weese/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7308284/2026/05/25/fat-joe-knicks-cavaliers-nba-playoffs-east-finals/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7308284/2026/05/25/fat-joe-knicks-cavaliers-nba-playoffs-east-finals/","articleBody":"The Cleveland Cavaliers weren’t going to allow New York’s celebrity row to commandeer their Rocket Arena courtside seats in Game 4 of the Eastern Conference finals.\nNot Fat Joe, and not even Spike Lee.\nThe rapper, whose real name is Joseph Cartagena, went on ESPN’s “NBA Today” in Cleveland before the game and said the organization revoked his ticket once it found out the purchaser was a known Knicks supporter.","headline":"Fat Joe says Cavaliers revoked his ticket to Game 4 vs. Knicks: ‘Shame on you all’","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:48:09+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:35:14+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/devon-henderson/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=675&fit=crop","contentUrl":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=675&fit=crop","width":1200,"height":675},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=900&fit=crop","contentUrl":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=900&fit=crop","width":1200,"height":900},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=1200&fit=crop","contentUrl":"https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25230309/GettyImages-2277577630.jpg?width=1200&height=1200&fit=crop","width":1200,"height":1200}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/pb4ZVhBOG5O1/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/pb4ZVhBOG5O1/","articleBody":"An engaging interview from Karl-Anthony Towns just now on ESPN Sportscenter.He admits the sweep and rest means there is a rust risk come Game 1 of the NBA Finals, whoever they’re playing. It’s something they have got to “figure out”.But the most compelling bits was his initial reaction to getting the Knicks to the NBA Finals:💬 “I mean, it’s an honour to even be in this position … with the team I grew up cheering for, my favourite team, and be in this position wearing this jersey, and to see the word hope be brought back to the city because of us.“I can’t lie, it’s something that's emotional and it’s something I’ve always dreamed of, and you never know if it’s gonna come true. “You always think you got to play 2K to reach these heights, but I’m super happy we have this opportunity to be back somewhere where the Knicks deserve to be.”","headline":"KAT emotional at Knicks achievement","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:46:48+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:45:18+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/michael-bailey/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/pb4ZVhBOG5O1_TjpuJ4idHQpF_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/yrPe2bN15zGT/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/yrPe2bN15zGT/","articleBody":"One of the coolest scenes of the evening is watching those in the buses, cars — and yes, even NYFD trucks — driving down 7th Avenue, taking out their phones and recording the historic night as they pass by.","headline":"One of the coolest scenes of the evening is watching those in the buses, cars — and yes, even NYFD t","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:40:08+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:40:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/charlotte-carroll/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/qr1QUbPztuON/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/qr1QUbPztuON/","articleBody":"New York fell in love with the 1970-73 Knicks because of their likability … in how they played and how they carried themselves. Brunson, KAT, Hart, Bridges, OG, Mike Brown, Shamet etc — they have that quality. Important part of this historic return to the NBA Finals.","headline":"2026 Knicks similar to 1970s","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:38:08+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:38:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/ian-oconnor/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/qr1QUbPztuON_qGXsg84OpZgQ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publisher":{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/#publisher"}},{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/cH8qsAYdroCO/","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/cH8qsAYdroCO/","articleBody":"The Knicks have not beaten the Thunder since Nov. 21, 2022. The Thunder’s starters in that game: Shai Gilgeous-Alexander, Lu Dort, Josh Giddey, Kenrich Williams and Jeremiah Robinson-Earl. That’s historically been a rough matchup for New York.They did, however, play the Spurs well this season, beating them in the NBA Cup final and smashing them at Madison Square Garden on March 1 by 25 points. That was one of four regular-season losses the Spurs had after Feb. 1; two of the other three were nailbiters to Denver, while the third was in the season finale when the Spurs rested their key players.The Spurs beat the Knicks in late December, but only by two points and only because Julian Champagnie hit 11 3s.So if you’re a Knicks fan hoping for a title, I’d recommend rooting for the Spurs in the West finals.","headline":"Looking ahead to the Finals","dateModified":"2026-05-26T03:35:08+00:00","datePublished":"2026-05-26T03:35:00+00:00","copyrightYear":2026,"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/author/mike-prada/#person"},"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=675,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":675,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=900,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":900,"creditText":"Getty Images"},{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","contentUrl":"https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1200,height=1200,fit=crop/8jKUFvbSM6rv_0PViFUOkhYyZ_1440x960.jpg","width":1200,"height":1200,"creditText":"Getty Images"}],"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/knicks-vs-cavaliers-live-updates-nba-playoffs-game-4-score-result/8jKUFvbSM6rv/","publish