0%27%20height=%2730%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%"/></span></div></div></div></div><div id="liveblog-post-content" class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogBody__9bgXM LiveBlogs_PostBody__HX1FM"><p>As one of the replies to this clip says, does this mean the Cleveland Cavaliers were also genuinely — as well as analytically — better than the Knicks?</p><p>Probably one for the 2026-27 NBA regular season now, James. </p></div><div><div class="Tweet_UnloadedTweet__njwA_ Tweet_IncludesMedia__OGUlN"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">“Genuinely, I do feel like we are the better team,” - James Harden after the Cavs were swept by the Knicks 🫨🫨🫨 <a href="https://t.co/JtDk8A7D2F">pic.twitter.com/JtDk8A7D2F</a></p>&mdash; ESPN Cleveland (@ESPNCleveland) <a href="https://twitter.com/ESPNCleveland/status/2059116208331342062?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">May 26, 2026</a>

</div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogContentSection__5VgoG"><div class="Fade_Base__oC3XN Fade_FadeIn__BlL3J" style="--fade-duration:1000ms"><div><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogPostContainer__gp4u6 LiveBlogs_BottomBorder__SPKpV"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostHeader__HRJXp"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostBylineContainer__GCAVS"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostHeader__HRJXp post-header-link"><div class="Avatar_Base__PEyFI styled-image-with-fallback" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;position:relative;width:40px;height:40px"><div class="image" style="position:relative;width:40px;height:40px;visibility:hidden"><div class="Image_Root--centered__66MeR"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%"><img style="display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0" alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20version=%271.1%27%20width=%2740%27%20height=%2740%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="Michael Bailey" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:cover"/><noscript><img alt="Michael Bailey" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;bord