Meta__he7PA"><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogNonRelativeTimestamp__K8_LD LiveBlogs_LiveBlogPostTimestamp__7iB7e"><time dateTime="2026-05-26T03:55:00.000Z">May 25, 2026<!-- --> at 11:55 PM<!-- --> EDT</time></div><div><div class="LiveBlogs_PostByline___riv_"><span class="nowrap">Fred Katz</span><span>·</span><span><div class="LineClamp_LineClamp__OYTvW" style="-webkit-line-clamp:1">Staff Writer, Knicks reporting from Rocket Arena</div></span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="LiveBlogs_PostActions__3TiJu"><div role="button" tabindex="0" style="cursor:pointer;display:inline-block" aria-label="Copy to Clipboard"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostLinkImage__9XocL post-link Image_Root--centered__66MeR"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%"><img style="display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0" alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20version=%271.1%27%20width=%2730%27%20height=%2730%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%"/></span></div></div></div></div><h2 class="LiveBlogs_PostTitle__v911d">Who is Brock Aller? The Brunson dealmaker</h2><figure style="margin:0"><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogImageContainer__nB2uM"><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogImage__QNL1Y"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;padding-top:66.66666666666666%"></span><img alt="Who is Brock Aller? The Brunson dealmaker" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" decoding="async" data-nimg="responsive" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%"/><noscript><img alt="Who is Brock Aller? The Brunson dealmaker" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="responsive" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%" class="image-next-root" sizes="
  (max-width: 600px) 90vw,
  (max-width: 700px) 100vw,
  700px
" srcSet="https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=600%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 600w, https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=770%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 770w, https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1000%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 1000w, https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1248%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 1248w, https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1440%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 1440w, https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1920%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg 1920w" src="https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1920%2cquality=70%2cformat=auto/https://cdn-media.theathletic.com/vKigkqlVOVs9_ZLNxXrTf5dlU_1440x960.jpg"/></noscript></span></div></div><figcaption><span class="LiveBlogs_ImageCaption__WXzt7"> </span><span class="LiveBlogs_ImageCredit__DYVtG" style="padding-bottom:0">Getty Images</span></figcaption></figure><div id="liveblog-post-content" class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogBody__9bgXM LiveBlogs_PostBody__HX1FM"><p>This Knicks regime’s first front-office hire was a little-known salary cap aficionado in Cleveland, <strong>Brock Aller</strong>.</p><p>Leon Rose might be first in charge. William Wesley might be second. In 2020, Scott Perry was third; now, it’s Gersson Rosas. But Aller, an obsessor of the margins, someone who former Cavaliers lead executive David Griffin dubbed a “diabolical genius,” makes more trade calls than anyone else in the organization.</p><p>And Aller adores his precious draft picks. One time, shortly after he joined the Knicks, Aller left an empty pizza box in his office for a curiously long time. A joke emerged in the building: That box must be where he stored the Knicks’ valuable first-rounders.</p><p>The Mavericks, even with the Knicks all-in on <strong>Jalen Brunson</strong>, could not flip the lid of that pizza box.</p><p>Four months later, after Brunson helped the Mavs to the conference finals, after Tom Thibodeau had hired Rick Brunson, they were rewarded.</p><p>Aller swindled deal after deal on 2022 draft night, garnering future draft picks and getting off enough salary to sign Brunson and more.</p><p>Four years later, Brunson is a three-time All-NBA member, the captain of a team that is just four victories short of inspiring New York City to combust.</p></div></div></div></div></section><div data-live-blog-ad-slot="true" class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogAdSlot__v90mV"><div class="ad-wrapper no-margin-ad"><a href="#after-mid0-3-ad" class="skip-link">SKIP ADVERTISEMENT</a><div class="ad-slug-container"><p class="slug ad-slug">Advertisement</p></div><div id="mid0-3" data-position="mid0-3" class="ad"></div><div id="after-mid0-3-ad" tabindex="-1"></div></div></div><section class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogContentSection__5VgoG"><div class="Fade_Base__oC3XN Fade_FadeIn__BlL3J" style="--fade-duration:1000ms"><div><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogPostContainer__gp4u6 LiveBlogs_BottomBorder__SPKpV"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostHeader__HRJXp"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostBylineContainer__GCAVS"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostHeader__HRJXp post-header-link"><div class="Avatar_Base__PEyFI styled-image-with-fallback" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;position:relative;width:40px;height:40px"><div class="image" style="position:relative;width:40px;height:40px;visibility:hidden"><div class="Image_Root--centered__66MeR"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%"><img style="display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0" alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20version=%271.1%27%20width=%2740%27%20height=%2740%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="Fred Katz" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:cover"/><noscript><img alt="Fred Katz" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:cover" class="image-next-root" srcSet="https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2018/09/21185530/Katz-Fred-Headshot-092018.jpg?width=48&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp 1x, https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2018/09/21185530/Katz-Fred-Headshot-092018.jpg?width=96&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp 2x" src="https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2018/09/21185530/Katz-Fred-Headshot-092018.jpg?width=96&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp"/></noscript></span></div></div></div><div class="LiveBlogs_PostMeta__he7PA"><div class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogNonRelativeTimestamp__K8_LD LiveBlogs_LiveBlogPostTimestamp__7iB7e"><time dateTime="2026-05-26T03:52:00.000Z">May 25, 2026<!-- --> at 11:52 PM<!-- --> EDT</time></div><div><div class="LiveBlogs_PostByline___riv_"><span class="nowrap">Fred Katz</span><span>·</span><span><div class="LineClamp_LineClamp__OYTvW" style="-webkit-line-clamp:1">Staff Writer, Knicks reporting from Rocket Arena</div></span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="LiveBlogs_PostActions__3TiJu"><div role="button" tabindex="0" style="cursor:pointer;display:inline-block" aria-label="Copy to Clipboard"><div class="LiveBlogs_PostLinkImage__9XocL post-link Image_Root--centered__66MeR"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%"><img style="display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0" alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20version=%271.1%27%20width=%2730%27%20height=%2730%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%"/></span></div></div></div></div><h2 class="LiveBlogs_PostTitle__v911d">Dolan’s role in recent Knicks run</h2><div id="liveblog-post-content" class="LiveBlogs_LiveBlogBody__9bgXM LiveBlogs_PostBody__HX1FM"><p>For years, people claimed the Knicks could never win as long as owner <strong>James Dolan</strong>, who was more hands-on in his early stage of owning the franchise, was at the top. </p><p>Those allegations can no longer exist, though the irony is that it took Dolan looking elsewhere for the front office to operate more autonomously.</p><p>In 2018, Dolan’s passion project began in Las Vegas, the construction of a high-tech, globe-like venue on the Strip that would change entertainment forever. The process of building his Sphere was bumpy. The venture climbed over budget, ending up with a $2.3-billion price tag, which diverted much of Dolan’s time to Vegas. Basketball dropped down the list of priorities.</p><p>Then the Sphere opened in 2023. He’s been around the team more since. Though his opinion was not the only factor in firing Tom Thibodeau just days after last year’s Eastern Conference finals, the deepest playoff run the Knicks had made in a quarter century, he spearheaded the coach’s ousting, <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7269240/2026/05/11/knicks-76ers-mike-brown-owner-james-dolan/" target=_self>as <em>The Athletic’s</em> Ian O’Connor detailed.</a></p><p>Now, after three clinical series and a constant stream of innovative, strategic adjustments from the new head coach, Mike Brown, the Knicks will play deeper into the spring than they have since Dolan’s first year at the helm.</p><p>The wager paid off.</p></div><div><a id="go-further-container" class="LiveBlogs_GoFurtherContainer__xhJNR" href="https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7307698/2026/05/25/knicks-nba-finals-jalen-brunson-james-dolan-leon-rose/"><div class="LiveBlogs_GoFurtherImageContainer__6bgRf"><div class="Image_Root--centered__66MeR"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%"><span style="box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%"><img style="display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0" alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg%20xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20version=%271.1%27%20width=%2764%27%20height=%2764%27/%3e"/></span><img alt="How the Knicks built an NBA Finals team: Patience, restraint and Jalen Brunson" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" class="image-next-root" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:cover"/><noscript><img alt="How the Knicks built an NBA Finals team: Patience, restraint and Jalen Brunson" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="intrinsic" style="border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:cover" class="image-next-root" srcSet="https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25221131/GettyImages-2270144782-scaled.jpg?width=64&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp 1x, https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25221131/GettyImages-2270144782-scaled.jpg?width=128&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp 2x" src="https://static01.nyt.com/athletic/uploads/wp/2026/05/25221131/GettyImages-2270144782-scaled.jpg?width=128&amp;quality=70&amp;auto=webp"/></noscript></span></div></div><div><p class="LiveBlogs_GoFurtherLabel__AgfXQ">GO FURTHER</p><p class="LiveBlogs_GoFurtherText__Wlbw_">How the Knicks built an NBA Finals team: Patience, restraint and Jalen Brunson</p></div></a></div></div></div></div></se